{%- comment -%}
  fye-pdx-delivery: the estimated delivery block under Add to bag on the
  redesigned product page (CRO handoff, 27/09/2026).

  The dates are computed IN THE BROWSER by fye-ui.js: today plus lead_min to
  lead_max working days, weekends skipped, printed "9–15 October" or
  "30 September – 2 October". Liquid cannot do this honestly, because the
  page is cached and "today" would be whenever it was last rendered. With JS
  off, the fallback says the same thing in working days.

  Bank holidays are NOT skipped. Across a holiday the window reads a day
  early; the range already absorbs that, and "Need it sooner?" is the escape.

  "Need it sooner?" opens the product enquiry popup, falling back to the
  Contact us popup's page when that popup is absent.

  unit: 'weeks' (rings, Ed 27/09/2026) counts WEEKS from the next working
  day: an order on a Friday evening starts on Monday, and 3 to 4 weeks from
  that Monday lands on a Monday. Without it, lead_min and lead_max are
  working days from today (loose stones).

  Parameters: lead_min, lead_max, unit (optional), sub (the line beneath)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign unit_words = 'working days'
  if unit == 'weeks'
    assign unit_words = 'weeks'
  endif
-%}
<div class="pdx__deliv" data-pdx-delivery data-min="{{ lead_min }}" data-max="{{ lead_max }}"{% if unit == 'weeks' %} data-unit="weeks"{% endif %}>
  <p class="pdx__delivwhen">Estimated delivery: <strong data-pdx-delivery-dates>{{ lead_min }}–{{ lead_max }} {{ unit_words }}</strong></p>
  {%- if sub != blank -%}
    <p class="pdx__delivsub">{{ sub }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
  <p class="pdx__delivsoon">Need it sooner? <a href="/pages/contact-us#popup-contact" data-fye-popup="pdx-enquire">Contact us here</a> and we may be able to accommodate you.</p>
</div>
